    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/kg-navigation.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why it is a package under `cat-harness/skills/`, and was not for three days",
      "prov:value": "From 2026-09-20 it was a top-level instance (`kg-navigation/`, with its own\n`kg-navigation.json`). That instance declared no `needs`, so when bean `j79e`\ngave `kg:detangle` a direction classifier, its edges could only be reported\nas **undetermined**: nothing said which layer it sat in. The owner's ruling,\n2026-09-23: *\"Make them visualization of an existing harness\"*, and of the\noptions, **fold into cat-harness**. Its layer is now cat-harness's.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean j79e",
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/kg-navigation.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why it is a package under `cat-harness/skills/`, and was not for three days",
      "prov:value": "The old argument against this location — *\"a nested entry would be a\ndeclaration inside a declaration\"* (#263) — was about a SECOND declaration.\nThere is none now: `skills/` owns this directory like every other package.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#263"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/kg-navigation.md#provenance-8",
